# Quality

- Format with Prettier. Do not bypass `format:check` in CI. CI stays
  check-only. Do not auto-commit from Actions or add
  `continue-on-error` on the Prettier job.
- When CI **Prettier** fails on a PR this agent opened or last pushed
  (including after a **human** GitHub conflict resolve / merge from
  `test`), in the **same turn**, without asking: `npm run format`,
  Conventional Commit (`style: apply Prettier`), `git push` that
  branch (new SHA). Do not wait for the human to paste the log or to
  say “format it”. Do not `gh run rerun` the old SHA. Follow
  `.cursor/skills/heal/SKILL.md`. CI stays check-only (no
  `--write` / auto-commit from Actions). Subscribe to CI on **each**
  such PR head, not only the latest branch in the chat.
- ESLint is required once application source exists. Until then, document the strategy; do not fake an app lint suite.
- Conventional Commits are required.
- Do not weaken GitHub Actions quality gates.
- Do not use `continue-on-error: true` on required CI jobs.
- Do not force-push to `test` or `main`.
